WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:03.630
- My mother who was, we
put her into a condo,

00:00:03.630 --> 00:00:04.650
as I could tell her.

00:00:04.650 --> 00:00:06.327
Her house all, she's short, so

00:00:06.327 --> 00:00:07.980
(Kelly laughing)

00:00:07.980 --> 00:00:09.305
all the pictures are real-

00:00:09.305 --> 00:00:10.138
- Is it assisted living?

00:00:10.138 --> 00:00:11.460
Is that what it is?

00:00:11.460 --> 00:00:13.920
- Ah, it's such a long story, so its-

00:00:13.920 --> 00:00:15.360
- I just love that you called it a condo.

00:00:15.360 --> 00:00:18.487
- The only way I could
get her in it is I said,

00:00:18.487 --> 00:00:20.280
"Hey, think of it as a condo."

00:00:20.280 --> 00:00:21.907
- And her whole demeanor says,

00:00:21.907 --> 00:00:23.917
"Oh, like in Florida or something?"

00:00:23.917 --> 00:00:25.325
"Yeah, that would be it

00:00:25.325 --> 00:00:26.158
(audience laughing)

00:00:26.158 --> 00:00:27.000
except it's in mid-Michigan.

00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:29.940
But, yeah, consider it
a condo in Florida."

00:00:29.940 --> 00:00:31.710
- But people take care
of you. That's nice.

00:00:31.710 --> 00:00:33.210
They play games, they do stuff.

00:00:33.210 --> 00:00:34.650
- Yeah, uh-huh.

00:00:34.650 --> 00:00:35.700
- Do you feel like it's your turn

00:00:35.700 --> 00:00:37.110
to take care of your momma now?

00:00:37.110 --> 00:00:40.230
- Well, nobody trains
you how to be a parent,

00:00:40.230 --> 00:00:42.150
and certainly nobody trains
you how to be a parent

00:00:42.150 --> 00:00:43.350
to your parent.

00:00:43.350 --> 00:00:45.000
- Yeah.
- Luckily there's nine of us,

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:48.120
and we're able to move,
all of us are, but it's-

00:00:48.120 --> 00:00:50.790
- I forget how many brothers
or siblings you have, wow.

00:00:50.790 --> 00:00:53.010
- Yeah, I'm lucky 'cause I
have a lot of good friends

00:00:53.010 --> 00:00:54.780
that are taking care of
their parents on their own,

00:00:54.780 --> 00:00:56.703
and it's so much.
- Yeah.

00:00:57.752 --> 00:00:58.620
- If you're doing it, or you see it,

00:00:58.620 --> 00:01:00.780
it's really difficult 'cause-

00:01:00.780 --> 00:01:02.370
- Well, it's time consuming
if you also have a job,

00:01:02.370 --> 00:01:04.020
and you also have a family until-

00:01:04.890 --> 00:01:06.180
- My mother once looked at me

00:01:06.180 --> 00:01:08.913
and I've had a good
relationship with my mom.

00:01:09.780 --> 00:01:11.070
I've been in a lot of trouble my life

00:01:11.070 --> 00:01:14.070
and so she and I have
come to understanding

00:01:14.070 --> 00:01:16.470
that none of my bad
behavior was her problem.

00:01:16.470 --> 00:01:18.120
I made my own bad decisions.

00:01:18.120 --> 00:01:19.290
And I've helped her through this,

00:01:19.290 --> 00:01:22.201
but, I've been like a friend of hers

00:01:22.201 --> 00:01:23.034
(Kelly laughing)

00:01:23.034 --> 00:01:24.240
'cause I listened to
everything she has to say

00:01:24.240 --> 00:01:25.560
and I don't give her any advice.

00:01:25.560 --> 00:01:28.380
And so, she's mean right
now to all my brothers.

00:01:28.380 --> 00:01:30.060
And she finally got mean to me one day.

00:01:30.060 --> 00:01:32.730
I was telling her, "You can't do this."

00:01:32.730 --> 00:01:33.720
She didn't make any sense.

00:01:33.720 --> 00:01:35.010
She's making weird sentences.

00:01:35.010 --> 00:01:35.843
And I said, "I don't understand."

00:01:35.843 --> 00:01:36.757
"You're calling me a liar!"

00:01:36.757 --> 00:01:37.650
"No, I didn't call you a liar,

00:01:37.650 --> 00:01:39.480
but the first part of that sentence

00:01:39.480 --> 00:01:41.040
did not match the last part."

00:01:41.040 --> 00:01:42.120
She goes, "You know what?

00:01:42.120 --> 00:01:44.667
Why don't you go to lunch
and don't hurry back."

00:01:44.667 --> 00:01:46.260
(Kelly and audience laughing)

00:01:46.260 --> 00:01:49.140
I laughed at first, I went,
(laughs) "Are you serious?

00:01:49.140 --> 00:01:50.607
Did you just say that to me?"

00:01:51.810 --> 00:01:54.960
She doesn't know how to shut things off.

00:01:54.960 --> 00:01:56.360
And it's a real challenge.
- Oh, my mom,

00:01:56.360 --> 00:02:00.120
she'll hate me for
this, she has no filter.

00:02:00.120 --> 00:02:02.054
Do not ask my mom for the truth.

00:02:02.054 --> 00:02:03.030
(Kelly and audience laughing)

00:02:03.030 --> 00:02:04.590
'Cause she will serve it up on a platter

00:02:04.590 --> 00:02:05.550
and be like, "You asked."

00:02:05.550 --> 00:02:06.750
- But you're not asking for it.

00:02:06.750 --> 00:02:09.090
That's what I'm saying-
- No, no, she does that too.

00:02:09.090 --> 00:02:10.290
You don't even have to ask.

00:02:10.290 --> 00:02:11.613
Yeah, she does that too.

